  "comments": "<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5da9d58e24b9d.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5da9d58e24b9d.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"150\" /></a><br /><br />\r\nNOTE 1: On Obverse, the lower left point of the bust points to the U (KM# 104.1) or the P (KM# 104.2) of the word REPUBLICA<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/60e10136a3b36.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/60e10136a3b36.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"150\" /></a><br />\r\nKM# 104.1 on right, KM# 104.2 on left<br />\r\n© adanieluy<br /><br />\r\nNOTE 2: On 2007, mintage was made at Paris where they copied the design from 1998 issue; by mistake, they assumed the Santiago Mintmark was part of the design and didn&#039;t remove it.<br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">Variants:</span><br />\r\nSeveral variants in this coin.<br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">1994:</span><br />\r\nRotation:<br />\r\nSA# 138.1.1, CG# 153.1.A, coin rotation,<br />\r\nSA# 138.1.2, CG# 153.1.B, medal rotation (normal issue),<br />\r\nSA# 138.1.3, CG# 153.1.C, 90º or 270º rotation,<br />\r\nSA# 138.1.4, CG# 153.1.D, other rotation.<br /><br />\r\nObverse:<br />\r\nDesign: length of hair on back, touching or not collar, lower right point of the bust points to center of &quot;U&quot;, or to its side, on last &quot;U&quot; of &quot;URUGUAY&quot;;<br />\r\ntypography: on &quot;DEL&quot; different shape of &quot;D&quot;, round and square; different length of lower part of &quot;L&quot;;<br />\r\nReverse:<br />\r\nFinishing: smooth background with thin letters, high relief, or rough background with bold letter, low relief.<br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">1998:</span><br />\r\nRotation:<br />\r\nSA# 142.1.2, CG# 162.1.B, medal rotation (normal issue),<br />\r\nSA# 142.1.3, CG# 162.1.C, 90º or 270º rotation,<br />\r\nSA# 142.1.4, CG# 162.1.D, other rotation.<br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">2007:</span><br />\r\nNo variations.",
